  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="fe456904-7008-50be-ad70-41908f6d256a" activityNameId="b4c83477-9578-59b7-8821-69f1a073d962" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Alkyd paint, white, 60% in H2O, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Alkyd paint, white, 60% in H2O, at plant
Alkyd paints can be made of many different resins. This dataset stands for one specific long oil alkyd as used in architectural paints of white colour and should not be used for other alkyds if it's contribution to the overall result is important. The data quality is not sufficient to allow for e.g. a comparative assessment of different paints.\nTechnology: The dataset models the commonly used process for water-reducible alkyd resin production. Paint production is done by physical mixing of resin, water and pigments.\nVersion: 2.2\nSynonyms: water-reducible, wasserlöslich\nEnergy values: Undefined\nProduction volume: unknown\nLocal category: Lacke &amp; Farben, Leime\nLocal subcategory: Herstellung\nUVEK 2022 source file:01669.XML\n\n
Synonyms: water-reducible, wasserlöslich; 
UUID: 4ae47809-79a6-30d0-b679-61fbb0beedf8
Transport of raw materials and production of paint. Packaging is neglected.
Location: undefined
Technology: The dataset models the commonly used process for water-reducible alkyd resin production. Paint production is done by physical mixing of resin, water and pigments.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: A "typical" water-reducible white alkyd paint is chosen and its raw material consumption is calcu-lated. Energy data are estimated. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4ae47809-79a6-30d0-b679-61fbb0beedf8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
